// critarea.rule -- SYNTHETIC (NO vendor data). Exercises shorts Critical-Area
// Analysis (fork feature #46): a circular particle defect of radius rho shorts two
// conductors iff its centre lies within rho of BOTH, i.e. inside (P_i (+)rho) AND
// (P_j (+)rho). The shorts critical area at a probe radius is the union of that locus
// over every distinct conductor pair (um^2).
//
// Layer numbers are synthetic placeholders:  met1 4/0.
//
//   CRITAREA <layer> RADIUS <rho> <cmp> <value>
//       measure the shorts critical area at defect radius <rho> and gate it.
//       KLayout's default (mode-2) sizing grows an orthogonal shape to an exact
//       rectangle, so for two parallel rails length L, spacing s this reduces to the
//       closed form  (2*rho - s) * (L + 2*rho)  -- hand-checkable to the DBU.
//       The defect-DENSITY weighting that turns this into a yield number is
//       foundry-[EXT] and stays a caller multiplier; here we ship the geometry engine.
//
// Two rails L=10, gap s, at rho=1.5:  CA = (3 - s) * 13.
//     s = 2.000 -> CA = 13.000   s = 1.999 -> CA = 13.013   s = 1.0 -> CA = 26.0
//     s = 4.0   -> 2*rho=3 < s   -> grown rails never meet -> CA = 0.0
//
// CA.M1.PASS gates > 13.0 (so s=2.000 PASSes at exactly the limit, s=1.999 FAILs);
// CA.M1.FAIL gates > 12.999 (so the s=2.000 CA of 13.0 FAILs and emits the marker).

LAYER met1 4 0

CA.M1.PASS {
  CRITAREA met1 RADIUS 1.5 > 13.0
}

CA.M1.FAIL {
  CRITAREA met1 RADIUS 1.5 > 12.999
}
